  "topic": "history",
  "summary": "In November 1980, Lake Peigneur drained into the Jefferson Island salt mine. The workers escaped and a canal reversed into the basin. The workers in the animation are fictional composites.",
  "narrative": {
    "premise": "An entire Louisiana lake goes down a hole in its own floor.",
    "stakes": "A drilling crew and underground miners have to escape while their work sites flood and collapse.",
    "mechanism": "Drilling appears to have connected water to the mine, and the collapsing ground widened the opening.",
    "analogy": "A bathtub plug is pulled, except the bathtub is a lake and the drain leads to a mine.",
    "callback": "Return to the quiet lake from the opening, now refilled, after the oil drill changed its plumbing."
